<!--
  One straight bracket at the top right and one speech-bubble corner at the bottom left.
  The bubble corner keeps the frame's two edges straight for a run (12dp each), then bends into a
  V — arms 11.2dp, apex angle 45 degrees — so the edges pinch out into a tail instead of
  turning a right angle. Stroke caps are butt, so the runs just stop.
  The glyph sits 1dp up and right of the true centre: the tail and the bracket weigh opposite
  corners differently, and that is where the whole reads as balanced.
  Every point stays within the central 66dp safe zone, and 3dp strokes match the nested glyph.
  The frame carries the colour over a white plate and the glyph stays black; the monochrome layer
  reads only the alpha, so one drawable still serves both.
-->
